{
  "_comment": "The licence of every Python package a Vexa image installs, keyed name==version (gate:licenses, P17 / ADR-0004). uv.lock carries no licence, so each row is read from PyPI for that exact version by `node scripts/check-python-licenses.mjs --refresh` (license_expression, else the license field, else the licence classifiers joined with AND) and then reviewed here; refresh adds missing rows and never rewrites one. Rows corrected by hand from the project's own licence file: requests-unixsocket (PyPI declares none; repository LICENSE is Apache-2.0), uv (dual MIT OR Apache-2.0, per its README), python-dateutil (Apache-2.0 for contributions after 2017-12-01, BSD-3-Clause before, per its LICENSE), numpy (PyPI says only \"BSD License\"; its LICENSE.txt is BSD-3-Clause, and the native libraries its wheels bundle are listed in NOTICE). `installs` records what each Dockerfile `pip install` line resolves to, since those packages are outside any lock.",
